Every clinician should explain an expected-prescribed-medication-presence to a patient.
Every clinician should explain an expected-unreported-drug-absence to a patient.
Every clinician should explain an expected-unreported-nonprescribed-controlled-substance-absence to a patient.
Every clinician should ask a nonjudgmental-prescribed-drug-use-question during a patient-discussion.
Every clinician should ask a nonjudgmental-other-drug-use-question during a patient-discussion.
Every clinician should ask a nonjudgmental-possible-unexpected-result-question during a patient-discussion.
